---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SpecialText } from "$lib/components/spell/special-text";
import { Signature } from "$lib/components/spell/signature";
import { MoveLeft } from "@lucide/astro";
---

<Layout>
  <section class="m-20 relative grid place-items-center h-75">
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none opacity-20"
      style="
      background:
        radial-gradient(ellipse at 35% 40%, rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.6) 0%, transparent 40%),
        radial-gradient(ellipse at 55% 30%, rgba(20, 184, 166, 0.5) 0%, transparent 35%),
        radial-gradient(ellipse at 70% 60%, rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.4) 0%, transparent 45%),
        radial-gradient(ellipse at 25% 70%, rgba(5, 150, 105, 0.35) 0%, transparent 40%),
        radial-gradient(ellipse at 60% 70%, rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.3) 0%, transparent 50%),
        linear-gradient(135deg,
          rgba(5, 150, 105, 0.8) 0%,
          rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.6) 20%,
          rgba(20, 184, 166, 0.5) 40%,
          rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.4) 60%,
          rgba(5, 150, 105, 0.3) 100%
        );
      filter: blur(60px);
    "
    >
    </div>

    <h1 class="text-5xl">
      <SpecialText client:visible>Are you a club?</SpecialText>
    </h1>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-20">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="font-mono uppercase pl-4 mt-4 hover:text-muted-foreground"
      data-button><MoveLeft class="inline" /> Go back</a
    >
    <p class="text-xl">
      If your answer is a big strong <strong>yes</strong> (assuming you're a club
      from Nido de Águilas), then the Coding Club has got news for you! <br
      /><br /> If your club needs a website done, or any digital tool made, don't
      hesitate to contact the Coding Club! We are constantly learning new things about
      programming in general and web development, and being a team with so many different
      people, interests, and talents, it's (almost) guaranteed that you'll be able
      to receive a product in the style you desire!
    </p>

    <div class="text-center">
      <p class="text-xl">Just contact</p>
      <p class="text-3xl">
        Zhai <span id="mail" class="cursor-pointer text-lg hover:brightness-75"
          >(fanhongmeng.zhai@students.nido.cl)</span
        >!
      </p>
      <p class="text-md text-muted-foreground" id="message">click to copy!</p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-xl">
      But before you make a request, please make sure to include the following
      items in your email!
    </p>

    <ul class="list-disc text-xl">
      <li>Your name</li>
      <li>Your club's name</li>
      <li>
        What your club does (be as detailed as you want, the more detailed the
        better)
      </li>
      <li>
        What function should the website have (is it to show off your club? does
        it need to have any tools built into it?)
      </li>
      <li>
        And if you already have a design in mind, tell us! If not, we can figure
        something out together.
      </li>
      <li>
        Aaaand if you already have a <a
          class="text-emerald-400 underline"
          href="https://www.figma.com/"
          target="_blank">Figma</a
        > file or any equivalent design mockup ready (wow), we'd really appreciate
        that (it makes our job wayyyy easier)!
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-xl mt-10">
      We (will) use Svelte and SvelteKit to build your projects, and we'll
      probably use a UI library in order to maintain consistency. You get to
      choose which one we use based on how much you like how they look. Most UI
      libraries' components are also customizable, so don't worry if they're
      just slightly off your taste. Here's some that I know about - check them
      out, and include in the email if you want to use any of these (or if you
      do not want any use of UI libraries in the product):
    </p>
    <table class="tg mt-10">
      <thead class="border-b border-emerald-400">
        <tr>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th>Link</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Flowbite</td>
          <td
            ><a href="https://flowbite-svelte.com/" target="_blank"
              >https://flowbite-svelte.com</a
            ></td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Skeleton</td>
          <td
            ><a href="https://www.skeleton.dev/" target="_blank"
              >https://www.skeleton.dev/</a
            ></td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>shadcn/ui</td>
          <td
            ><a href="https://shadcn-svelte.com/" target="_blank">
              https://shadcn-svelte.com/
            </a></td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>DaisyUI</td>
          <td
            ><a href="https://daisyui.com/" target="_blank">
              https://daisyui.com/
            </a></td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>stdf</td>
          <td
            ><a href="https://stdf.dev/" target="_blank">
              https://stdf.dev/
            </a></td
          >
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-xl mt-10">
      And that's it! I'll respond to you within a day or two (including
      weekends, probably) and we can talk then. Do keep in mind that the website
      will NOT be the same quality as a if a professional software development
      firm had made it. Of course, if you need changes made to polish and make
      the website more to your liking, we'd be happy to do that, but please
      don't expect high school students some with less than a year of
      programming experience to produce a masterpiece.
    </p>
    <div class="flex items-center justify-center flex-col mt-10">
      <Signature
        client:load
        once
        text="Fanhongmeng Zhai"
        fontSize={16}
        color="#F0F0F0"
      />
      <hr class="w-64 h-0.5 -mt-8 bg-white" />
      <p>Fanhongmeng Zhai - Club Leader</p>
      <p class="mt-10">
        here's a fake signature to make everything look more official :)
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .tg td {
    padding: 2.5px 7.5px;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const mail = document.querySelector("#mail");
  const message = document.querySelector("#message");
  mail?.addEventListener("click", async (_e) => {
    if (!message) {
      console.error("Could not find message element!");
      return;
    }

    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText("fanhongmeng.zhai@students.nido.cl");

      message.innerHTML = "copied!";

      setTimeout(() => {
        message.innerHTML = "click to copy!";
      }, 2000);

      console.log("Succesfully copied email to clipboard!");
    } catch (err) {
      console.error("Failed to copy email to clipboard!");
    }
  });
</script>
